<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Vanuatu</h1><p class="st-meta">1980 CE – present · capital Port Vila</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Melanesian archipelago republic, independent in 1980 after an Anglo-French condominium, with three official languages and frequently changing governments.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-hebrides-condominium">New Hebrides Condominium</a> was jointly managed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the United Kingdom from 1906. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanuaaku-pati">Vanua'aku Pati</a> won the 1979 elections, and independence came on 30 July 1980 under Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walter-lini">Walter Lini</a>, with a ceremonial president replacing the Resident Commissioners. Before independence, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagriamel">Nagriamel</a> movement under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimmy-stevens">Jimmy Stevens</a> took over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/espiritu-santo">Espiritu Santo</a> and declared the Republic of Vemarana.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Lini called in troops from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papua-new-guinea">Papua New Guinea</a>, and in the brief Coconut War they put down the Vemarana revolt; Stevens surrendered on 1 September 1980. Lini governed until a no-confidence vote on 6 September 1991, running an Anglophone-dominated government and joining the Non-Aligned Movement. Since then coalitions have been fractious and no-confidence votes have brought frequent changes of prime minister. The economy depends on beef, copra, tourism and remittances. Cyclone Pam in 2015 caused 16 deaths and great destruction.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Charlot Salwai became prime minister after the 2016 election and Bob Loughman after the 2020 election. A magnitude 7.3 earthquake in December 2024 damaged almost every house on Efate and killed 19 people. Vanuatu enacted the Vanuatu Oceans Act in November 2025, formalising community-based management of its marine resources.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/vanuatu.jpg" alt="Vanuatu" width="330" height="198"><figcaption>Image: Kalontas Mahlon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Vanuatu.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1980 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Port Vila</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Walter Lini, Maxime Carlot Korman, Ham Lini, Charlot Salwai, Bob Loughman</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity: Presbyterian, Roman Catholic, Anglican</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bislama, English, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/vanuatu">Vanuatu</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Vanuatu, New Hebrides</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2003&amp;focus=vanuatu" aria-label="Vanuatu on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: where Vanuatu lay"><image href="/maps/globes/g180s30.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4055 4007L4055 4007"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4055 4007h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4055 4007h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4055 4007h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Port Vila. <a href="/atlas?year=2003&amp;focus=vanuatu">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
